.TH fleetring-db 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-db \- Creates, lists, writes, reads, watches, and drops databases
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring db\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates, lists, writes, reads, watches, and drops databases
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-db\-create(1)
Creates a SQLite database, places it with the ring, and opens it on its primary
.TP
fleetring\-db\-show(1)
Shows a database in detail: placement, description, labels, expiry, schema
.TP
fleetring\-db\-edit(1)
Changes a database\*(Aqs description, labels, expiry, or durability
.TP
fleetring\-db\-exec(1)
Runs one write statement on the database\*(Aqs primary
.TP
fleetring\-db\-query(1)
Runs one read\-only query on the database\*(Aqs primary
.TP
fleetring\-db\-watch(1)
Follows a database\*(Aqs row changes, one transaction per line, until Ctrl\-C
.TP
fleetring\-db\-locate(1)
Shows where a database lives: its primary, followers, and epoch
.TP
fleetring\-db\-list(1)
Lists the databases, with their placement and durability
.TP
fleetring\-db\-verify(1)
Checks that every replica of a database holds the same log
.TP
fleetring\-db\-restore(1)
Creates a new database from an archived one
.TP
fleetring\-db\-drop(1)
Drops a database for good
